**Answer. **The UVM factory creates registered objects and components and applies overrides at creation time. type_id::create() asks the factory which implementation to instantiate; new() calls the named class constructor directly. I use create() for replaceable verification components and transactions, and new() for helper objects whose exact type is intentional.

```systemverilog
// packet uses `uvm_object_utils(packet).
packet p = packet::type_id::create("p");
// driver uses `uvm_component_utils(driver).
drv = driver::type_id::create("drv", this);
// Direct construction bypasses factory overrides.
p = new("p");
```

Register the replacement and set the override before creation. create() does not modify objects that already exist. Reference: [UVM factory reference](https://github.com/accellera-official/uvm-core/blob/main/src/base/uvm_factory.svh)

