**Key idea:** The test configures and starts sequences. The env holds agents plus the checking layer. Each active agent has a sequencer, driver, and monitor. The driver pulls items with `get_next_item`/`item_done`. Monitors publish what actually happened to the predictor, scoreboard, and coverage through analysis ports.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph TEST["test"]
    subgraph ENV["env"]
      subgraph AIN["input agent (active)"]
        SQR["sequencer"] --> DRV["driver"]
        IMON["monitor"]
      end
      subgraph AOUT["output agent (passive)"]
        OMON["monitor"]
      end
      PRED["predictor / ref model"]
      SCB["scoreboard"]
      COV["coverage"]
    end
  end
  SEQ["sequence"] -->|start_item / finish_item| SQR
  DRV -->|vif| DUT["DUT"]
  DUT -->|vif| IMON
