```systemverilog
class even_then_odd;
  rand int n;
  rand int unsigned a[];
  constraint c {
    n inside {[1:32]};
    a.size() == 2*n;
    foreach (a[i]) {
      if (i < n) a[i][0] == 0;
      else       a[i][0] == 1;
    }
  }
endclass
// For repeating groups, replace the if/else with:
// a[i][0] == ((i / n) % 2);
```

solution:
**Key idea:** Make the array size `2*n` and constrain the LSB by position: indices `< n` get `a[i][0] == 0` (even) and indices `>= n` get `a[i][0] == 1` (odd). Solve `n` first. It happens automatically, because sizes are solved before elements.

| n=3 | idx 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| region | even | even | even | odd | odd | odd |
| example | 8 | 42 | 0 | 17 | 5 | 99 |

### Solution
```systemverilog
class even_then_odd;
  rand int unsigned n;
  rand int unsigned a[];
  constraint c_size { n inside {[1:32]}; a.size() == 2 * n; }
  constraint c_par  {
    foreach (a[i]) {
      a[i] inside {[0:999]};
      if (i < n) a[i][0] == 1'b0;     // even
      else       a[i][0] == 1'b1;     // odd
    }
  }
endclass

module tb;
  initial begin
    even_then_odd e = new();
    if (!e.randomize()) $fatal(1, "randomize failed");
    $display("n=%0d a=%p", e.n, e.a);
  end
endmodule
```

### Explanation
- Variant with **repeating groups** of N even then N odd (`E E E O O O E E E ...`): use `a[i][0] == (i / n) % 2;` with any array size.
- Variant with a **fixed** N and 2N elements: drop `rand` from `n`.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- `n` must be `rand` if it appears in `a.size() == 2*n` and you want it chosen. As a non-rand state variable it's just an input.
- Using `int` (signed) `n` without a lower bound lets the solver try negative sizes and fail. Bound it.

### Follow-ups
- *Strictly increasing within each half?* Add `if (i > 0 && i != n) a[i] > a[i-1];`.
- *Alternate even/odd?* `a[i][0] == i[0];`.

