solution:
**Key idea:** A sequence item carries random *request* fields with legality constraints and non-random, four-state *observed* fields (so an X from the DUT stays visible). Nested objects need an explicit copy rule, and checkers compare only the fields that matter.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  SEQ["sequence<br/>randomize request fields"] --> DRV["driver<br/>fills rdata, status"]
  DRV -->|"item_done(rsp)"| SEQ
  MON["monitor<br/>new item per transfer"] -->|analysis port| SCB["scoreboard<br/>compares chosen fields"]
```

### Explanation
Interview answer: "Request fields are `rand` and carry legality constraints. Response fields like `rdata` are `logic` and not random, so an X from the DUT stays visible. I register fields with the factory, and I compare only the fields that matter instead of the generic `compare()`."

| Field | Kind | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `addr`, `wdata`, `write`, `strb` | `rand bit` | stimulus, constrained to legal values |
| `rdata` | `logic` (not rand) | X/Z from DUT must stay visible |
| `status` | enum, not rand | OK / ERR / RESET filled by driver or monitor |

### Code
```systemverilog
typedef enum {APB_OK, APB_ERR, APB_RESET} apb_status_e;

class apb_item extends uvm_sequence_item;
  rand bit [31:0] addr, wdata;
  rand bit        write;
  rand bit [3:0]  strb;
  logic [31:0]    rdata;      // observed, four-state
  apb_status_e    status;     // observed

  constraint legal_c {
    addr[1:0] == 0;
    addr inside {[32'h0:32'h3fc]};
    if (!write) strb == 0;
  }

  `uvm_object_utils_begin(apb_item)
    `uvm_field_int(addr,  UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(wdata, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(write, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(strb,  UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(rdata, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_enum(apb_status_e, status, UVM_DEFAULT)
  `uvm_object_utils_end

  function new(string name = "apb_item");
    super.new(name);
    status = APB_RESET;
  endfunction
endclass

// DMA descriptor: a copy command, not a bus beat
class dma_item extends uvm_sequence_item;
  rand bit [31:0]   src, dst;
  rand int unsigned nbytes;
  constraint legal_c {
    nbytes inside {[4:4096]};
    nbytes % 4 == 0;
    src[1:0] == 0; dst[1:0] == 0;
    (longint'(src) + nbytes) <= 64'h1_0000_0000;   // no 32-bit wrap
    (longint'(dst) + nbytes) <= 64'h1_0000_0000;
    ((longint'(src) + nbytes) <= longint'(dst)) ||  // no overlap
    ((longint'(dst) + nbytes) <= longint'(src));
  }
  `uvm_object_utils_begin(dma_item)
    `uvm_field_int(src,    UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(dst,    UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(nbytes, UVM_DEFAULT)
  `uvm_object_utils_end
  function new(string name = "dma_item"); super.new(name); endfunction
endclass
```

**Trace:** `src=0x100, dst=0x200, nbytes=16` predicts four word writes to 0x200..0x20C. `dst=0x108` overlaps `[0x100,0x110)` and must fail randomization. The `longint'` casts stop `src + nbytes` from wrapping at 32 bits and silently satisfying the constraint.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- Field macros are convenient but slow and hide behavior; production code often hand-writes `do_copy`/`do_compare`.
- Error injection: a negative-test subclass, or `item.legal_c.constraint_mode(0)`.
- Expected DMA destination data is *predicted* from a source snapshot when the copy starts, never randomized.

### Follow-ups
- *copy vs clone?* `copy()` fills an existing object; `clone()` = `create()` + `copy()` and returns `uvm_object` (needs `$cast`).
- *Component vs object?* Components are static hierarchy with phases; objects are transient data.

