solution:
**Key idea:** Key both streams on something the monitor can observe (reset epoch, port, ID). Each key holds an expected FIFO and an actual FIFO, so either side may arrive first. Match when both are non-empty, compare spec-defined fields, time out stale entries, and require both tables empty at end of test.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  PRED["predictor"] -->|write_exp| EQ["expected[key] FIFO"]
  MON["output monitor"] -->|write_act| AQ["actual[key] FIFO"]
  EQ --> M{"both non-empty?"}
  AQ --> M
  M -->|yes| CMP["pop both, compare fields"]
  M -->|no| WAIT["wait; watchdog checks age"]
  CMP --> CHK["check_phase: tables empty"]
```

### Explanation
| Ordering | Structure |
| --- | --- |
| strict in order | one expected FIFO + one actual FIFO |
| reorder across IDs, in order per ID | queue per ID |
| reorder within an ID | need another observable key; never invent a sequence number the monitor cannot see |

### Code
```systemverilog
`uvm_analysis_imp_decl(_exp)
`uvm_analysis_imp_decl(_act)

class ooo_scoreboard extends uvm_scoreboard;
  `uvm_component_utils(ooo_scoreboard)
  uvm_analysis_imp_exp #(bus_item, ooo_scoreboard) exp_imp;
  uvm_analysis_imp_act #(bus_item, ooo_scoreboard) act_imp;

  typedef struct { bus_item t; time ts; } entry_t;
  entry_t exp_q[string][$];
  entry_t act_q[string][$];
  int unsigned epoch, matched, mismatched;
  time latency_bound = 10us;

  function new(string name, uvm_component parent);
    super.new(name, parent);
    exp_imp = new("exp_imp", this);
    act_imp = new("act_imp", this);
  endfunction

  function string key_of(bus_item t);
    return $sformatf("%0d/%0d/%0d", epoch, t.port, t.id);
  endfunction

  function void write_exp(bus_item t);
    bus_item c;
    $cast(c, t.clone());                 // own a copy
    exp_q[key_of(c)].push_back('{c, $time});
    match(key_of(c));
  endfunction

  function void write_act(bus_item t);
    bus_item c;
    $cast(c, t.clone());
    act_q[key_of(c)].push_back('{c, $time});
    match(key_of(c));
  endfunction

  function void match(string k);
    entry_t e, a;
    while (exp_q.exists(k) && act_q.exists(k) &&
           exp_q[k].size() > 0 && act_q[k].size() > 0) begin
      e = exp_q[k].pop_front();
      a = act_q[k].pop_front();
      if (e.t.data !== a.t.data) begin   // compare only spec-defined fields
        mismatched++;
        `uvm_error("MISMATCH", $sformatf("key %s exp=%h act=%h", k, e.t.data, a.t.data))
      end else matched++;
    end
    if (exp_q.exists(k) && exp_q[k].size() == 0) exp_q.delete(k);
    if (act_q.exists(k) && act_q[k].size() == 0) act_q.delete(k);
  endfunction

  task run_phase(uvm_phase phase);      // watchdog checks BOTH sides
    forever begin
      #1us;
      foreach (exp_q[k]) foreach (exp_q[k][i])
        if ($time - exp_q[k][i].ts > latency_bound)
          `uvm_error("TIMEOUT", $sformatf("expected %s never arrived", k))
      foreach (act_q[k]) foreach (act_q[k][i])
        if ($time - act_q[k][i].ts > latency_bound)
          `uvm_error("TIMEOUT", $sformatf("actual %s has no prediction", k))
    end
  endtask

  function void flush_on_reset();       // call from a reset event
    exp_q.delete(); act_q.delete(); epoch++;
  endfunction

  function void check_phase(uvm_phase phase);
    if (exp_q.num() || act_q.num())
      `uvm_error("LEFTOVER", $sformatf("%0d expected / %0d actual keys unmatched",
                                       exp_q.num(), act_q.num()))
  endfunction
endclass
```
(The watchdog reports repeatedly for a stuck entry; a real one would report once and remove it.)

### Adapting the template
- **Pipelined adder, strict order:** one queue; predict `{1'b0,a} + {1'b0,b}` only when the input is accepted; stalls create nothing.
- **Duplicates:** with unique tokens keep a set of retired tokens; with reusable IDs you need a spec rule. A leftover at timeout is not proof of a duplicate.
- **Split/reassemble (512-bit over 64-bit = 8 beats):** track expected length, a beat bitmap, byte enables, last marker; reject duplicate/out-of-range beats; compare only when complete.
- **Leading drop / garbage bits:** define the alignment rule (e.g. first byte after the start marker) and discard in the model, not the comparator.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- Two predictions with ID 3 need two queue entries, not an overwritten array slot.
- An unmatched actual must fail end-of-test even when the expected table is empty.

### Follow-ups
- *Why copy on arrival?* Publishers share one handle; a later modification would change stored entries.

