**Key idea:** The register model mirrors the DUT's registers. Frontdoor accesses go through an adapter and the real bus (testing address decode), backdoor accesses touch the HDL path directly (inspecting storage), and a predictor keeps the mirror in sync with monitored traffic. Comparing the two paths exposes decode and aliasing bugs.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant SEQ as reg sequence
  participant REG as uvm_reg
  participant ADP as adapter
  participant SQR as bus sequencer
  participant DRV as driver
  participant MON as monitor
  participant PRD as uvm_reg_predictor
  SEQ->>REG: ctrl.write(status, 32'h1)
  REG->>ADP: reg2bus(uvm_reg_bus_op)
  ADP-->>REG: bus item
  REG->>SQR: start_item / finish_item
  SQR->>DRV: get_next_item
  DRV->>DRV: drive pins
  MON->>PRD: analysis write(bus item)
  PRD->>ADP: bus2reg(item, rw)
  PRD->>REG: do_predict (update mirror)
```

