**Key idea:** Represent every region as half-open `[start, end)` with `end = start + length` computed in a wider type. Two regions do not overlap when one ends at or before the other starts; alignment is `start % align == 0`.

| Region A `[s,e)` | Region B `[s,e)` | `eA <= sB || eB <= sA` | Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [0x00, 0x20) | [0x20, 0x40) | 0x20 <= 0x20 true | adjacent, legal |
| [0x00, 0x21) | [0x20, 0x40) | false, false | overlap |
| [0x3E0, 0x400) | end = 1024 | fits `<= 1024` | fills the space exactly |
| start 0xFFFF_FFF0, len 0x20 | 32-bit end wraps to 0x10 | `longint'` end = 0x1_0000_0010 | must be rejected |

Alignment pitfall: for alignment 6, address 8 gives `8 & 5 = 0` (mask test passes) but `8 % 6 = 2` (not aligned). Masks work only for powers of two.

### Code
```systemverilog
class region_gen #(int N = 4);
  rand bit [31:0] start[N];
  rand bit [31:0] len[N];
  constraint regions_c {
    foreach (start[i]) {
      len[i] inside {[1:256]};
      start[i] % 32 == 0;
      longint'(start[i]) + len[i] <= 1024;          // widen before adding
    }
    foreach (start[i]) foreach (start[j])
      if (i < j) (longint'(start[i]) + len[i] <= start[j]) ||
                 (longint'(start[j]) + len[j] <= start[i]);
  }
endclass

// Excluded range
//   constraint ex_c { !(addr inside {[EX_LO:EX_HI]}); }

// Allocate repeatedly until full: remember previous regions
class allocator;
  bit [31:0] used_s[$], used_e[$];   // non-random history
  rand bit [31:0] s, l;
  constraint c {
    l inside {[1:64]};
    s % 32 == 0;
    longint'(s) + l <= 1024;
    foreach (used_s[k]) (longint'(s) + l <= used_s[k]) || (used_e[k] <= s);
  }
  function void post_randomize();
    used_s.push_back(s);
    used_e.push_back(s + l);
  endfunction
endclass
// loop: while (a.randomize()) ...;  // stops when the space is full (randomize returns 0)
```

### Rules to quote
- `end` is exclusive; adjacency `end_i == start_j` is legal.
- 2D rectangles do not overlap when one is completely left, right, above, or below: `x1+w1 <= x2 || x2+w2 <= x1 || y1+h1 <= y2 || y2+h2 <= y1`.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- Zero length (decide whether legal), a region filling the space exactly, wraparound at the top address, touching but not overlapping regions.
- Mixing inclusive ends (`start + len - 1`) with exclusive comparisons causes off-by-one overlaps.

### Follow-ups
