Blocking vs nonblocking pipeline (`in` = 1, 2, 3 on successive edges, all regs start at 0):

| edge | blocking `A=in; B=A; C=B;` (A,B,C) | nonblocking `A<=in; B<=A; C<=B;` (A,B,C) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 1, 1, 1 | 1, 0, 0 |
| 2 | 2, 2, 2 | 2, 1, 0 |
| 3 | 3, 3, 3 | 3, 2, 1 |

Blocking collapses to one register; nonblocking forms a three-stage shift register.

