### Code
```systemverilog
class region_alloc;
  int unsigned SPACE = 256, ALIGN = 16, MIN_SZ = 16, MAX_SZ = 64;
  int unsigned used_base[$], used_size[$];        // allocated so far (state, not rand)

  rand int unsigned base, size;

  constraint c_size  { size inside {[MIN_SZ:MAX_SZ]}; size % ALIGN == 0; }
  constraint c_fit   { base % ALIGN == 0; base <= SPACE - size; }   // no overflow: size <= SPACE
  constraint c_disj  {
    foreach (used_base[i])
      (base + size <= used_base[i]) || (base >= used_base[i] + used_size[i]);
  }

  // Largest free gap, computed independently of the solver
  function int unsigned largest_gap();
    int unsigned cur = 0, best = 0;
    int idx[$] = {};
    foreach (used_base[i]) idx.push_back(i);
    idx.sort() with (used_base[item]);
    foreach (idx[k]) begin
      best = (used_base[idx[k]] - cur > best) ? used_base[idx[k]] - cur : best;
      cur  = used_base[idx[k]] + used_size[idx[k]];
    end
    return (SPACE - cur > best) ? SPACE - cur : best;
  endfunction

  function void fill();
    while (largest_gap() >= MIN_SZ) begin
      if (!randomize())
        $fatal(1, "randomize failed although a gap of %0d >= MIN_SZ exists", largest_gap());
      used_base.push_back(base);
      used_size.push_back(size);
      $display("alloc [%0h, %0h)", base, base + size);
    end
    $display("done: %0d regions, used %0d of %0d", used_base.size(),
             used_size.sum(), SPACE);
  endfunction
endclass

module tb;
  initial begin
    region_alloc ra = new();
    ra.fill();
  end
endmodule
```

### Explanation
- Termination is based on an **independent** free-space computation, so a randomize failure while a fitting gap exists is reported as a real error instead of being mistaken for "full".
- Because sizes are multiples of `ALIGN` and `MIN_SZ == ALIGN`, any gap ≥ 16 can always be filled → this configuration does fill completely; with `MIN_SZ = 32` it can end with unusable 16-B holes.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- Updating the list before checking `randomize()` corrupts state with a stale/illegal region.
- `base + size` with narrow types can wrap — bounded here by `base <= SPACE - size`.
- Solver cost grows linearly with the number of prior regions; for thousands of regions use a free-list allocator and randomize only the choice of free block.

### Follow-ups
