### Corner cases & pitfalls
- **ID reuse**: if the DUT must not reuse an ID until the response comes back, flag a request whose ID is already outstanding (when only one per ID is allowed).
- **Timeouts**: store the request time and periodically check `$time - t_req > MAX_LAT`.
- **Reset**: flush `exp_q` on reset, otherwise every in-flight request becomes a false leftover error.
- Store a **copy** (`clone`) of the transaction; the monitor may reuse the handle.

