- **Checks**:
  - DUT error counter equals the number of bits the injector flipped (exact count when injecting 0, 1, N, and saturation value).
  - Hardware training (if the DUT sweeps by itself) picks the same center as the model.
  - Errors above threshold trigger the retrain interrupt; below threshold they do not.
- **Coverage**: eye position (near code 0, near max, wrap), eye width (1 code, wide), no eye, error counter saturation.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- Two separate passing windows: choose the widest, and define tie-breaking.
- PRBS checker lock: the first bits after enabling may be counted as errors until the checker self-synchronizes; exclude a lock time.
- Errors injected during settle time must not be counted.

