**Key idea:** the most recent unclosed opener must be closed first: last in, first out, i.e. a **stack**. Push openers, pop on a matching closer, fail on a mismatch or an empty stack, and require an empty stack at the end.

Trace `"([)]"`:

| char | action | stack after |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ( | push | ( |
| [ | push | ( [ |
| ) | top is `[`, want `(` | **mismatch: false** |

Trace `"{[()]}"`: push `{`, `[`, `(`; then `)`, `]`, `}` each match the top and pop; stack empty: **true**.

### Code
```cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

bool balanced(const string& s) {
    vector<char> st;                              // vector as a stack
    for (char c : s) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') {
            st.push_back(c);
        } else if (c == ')' || c == ']' || c == '}') {
            char want = (c == ')') ? '(' : (c == ']') ? '[' : '{';
            if (st.empty() || st.back() != want) return false;
            st.pop_back();
        }                                         // other chars ignored
    }
    return st.empty();                            // "((" fails here
}
```

