**Key idea:** one FIFO **per ID**. Expected items queue up under their ID; an actual item is compared with the **front** of its ID's queue. That enforces in-order within an ID while letting IDs complete in any order.

| event | exp_ after | check |
| --- | --- | --- |
| expected (1, 0xA) | 1: [A] | |
| expected (2, 0xB) | 1: [A], 2: [B] | |
| expected (1, 0xC) | 1: [A, C], 2: [B] | |
| actual (2, 0xB) | 1: [A, C], 2: [] | match (ID 2 overtook ID 1: legal) |
| actual (1, 0xC) | 1: [C] | **mismatch: exp A, got C** (same-ID reorder) |
| actual (3, 0xD) | | **unexpected id 3** |
| check_empty | 1: [C] left | **missing 1 response** |

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  REF["reference model"] -->|write_expected| MAP["map: id to deque of expected"]
  MON["monitor"] -->|write_actual| CMP["compare with front of deque[id]"]
  MAP --> CMP
  CMP --> ERR["errors++ on mismatch or unexpected id"]
  MAP --> END["check_empty: leftovers are dropped responses"]
```

### Code
```cpp
#include <unordered_map>
#include <deque>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstdio>
using namespace std;

class Scoreboard {
    unordered_map<int, deque<uint32_t>> exp_;
public:
    int errors = 0, matches = 0;

    void write_expected(int id, uint32_t data) { exp_[id].push_back(data); }

    void write_actual(int id, uint32_t data) {
        auto it = exp_.find(id);                 // find: don't create the key
        if (it == exp_.end() || it->second.empty()) {
            printf("ERROR unexpected id=%d data=0x%x\n", id, data);
            errors++;
            return;
        }
        uint32_t e = it->second.front();
        it->second.pop_front();
        if (e != data) {
            printf("ERROR id=%d exp=0x%x act=0x%x\n", id, e, data);
            errors++;
        } else {
            matches++;
        }
    }

    void check_empty() {                         // end-of-test (check_phase)
        for (const auto& [id, q] : exp_)
            if (!q.empty()) {
                printf("ERROR id=%d missing %zu responses\n", id, q.size());
                errors++;
            }
    }
};
```

